    {"id":"LEARN-PR154-032","pr":154,"source":"external_review","review_comment_id":4019702423,"class_id":"ADV-GUARDRAIL-ATTESTATION-GAP","invariant_ids":["INV-LEARNING-002"],"root_cause":"The trusted issue_comment workflow materialized only the implementation-scope wrapper while the wrapper resolved its shared scope core relative to its own temporary location. Real scope attestation therefore failed at import time instead of evaluating the candidate.","horizontal_audit":["trusted evaluator package materialization","wrapper-to-core locality","exact-base Git object provenance","temporary evaluator directory","candidate checkout remains data-only","scope command real execution path"],"guardrails":[{"path":"tools/assurance/test_validate_g1_identity_tenant_shell_authorization.py","probe":"falsify_trusted_scope_readiness_execution"}],"systemic_guardrail_updated":true,"guardrail_generation":145},
    {"id":"LEARN-PR154-033","pr":154,"source":"external_review","review_comment_id":4019702429,"class_id":"ADV-SEMANTIC-ALLOWLIST-BYPASS","invariant_ids":["INV-BOUNDARY-002","INV-OBS-002"],"root_cause":"The structural persistence-write detector recognized only direct known receiver spellings and an incomplete bracket-member shape. Aliasing a persistence receiver or using quoted computed-member invocation could perform G2-owned writes while semantic scope still passed.","horizontal_audit":["persistence receiver aliases","transitive simple aliases","dot member writes","quoted bracket member writes","destructured write methods","composition-only persistence boundary"],"guardrails":[{"path":"tools/assurance/test_validate_g1_identity_tenant_shell_authorization.py","probe":"falsify_implementation_scope_gate_execution"}],"systemic_guardrail_updated":true,"guardrail_generation":146},
    {"id":"LEARN-PR154-034","pr":154,"source":"external_review","review_comment_id":4019702438,"class_id":"ADV-SEMANTIC-ALLOWLIST-BYPASS","invariant_ids":["INV-BOUNDARY-002","INV-OBS-002"],"root_cause":"Raw-secret data-flow protection relied on a short sink vocabulary and therefore missed ordinary API response methods such as reply.send. A raw provider credential could be returned to the browser without matching the structural exposure fence.","horizontal_audit":["response send/json/end sinks","return-object secret exposure","log and print sinks","persistence sinks","raw password/token/credential flow","opaque credential_binding_ref regression"],"guardrails":[{"path":"tools/assurance/test_validate_g1_identity_tenant_shell_authorization.py","probe":"falsify_implementation_scope_gate_execution"}],"systemic_guardrail_updated":true,"guardrail_generation":147},
    {"id":"LEARN-PR154-035","pr":154,"source":"external_review","review_comment_id":4019702445,"class_id":"ADV-SEMANTIC-ALLOWLIST-BYPASS","invariant_ids":["INV-BOUNDARY-002","INV-OBS-002"],"root_cause":"Structural SQL hardening enumerated TABLE and SCHEMA but did not treat all DDL object classes as forbidden G2-owned persistence authority. CREATE OR REPLACE VIEW could therefore modify the shared Monitoring schema from a non-SQL artifact.","horizontal_audit":["CREATE OR REPLACE VIEW","materialized view","index sequence type function procedure trigger extension policy","ALTER and DROP variants","comment stripping","shared Monitoring read-only boundary"],"guardrails":[{"path":"tools/assurance/test_validate_g1_identity_tenant_shell_authorization.py","probe":"falsify_implementation_scope_gate_execution"}],"systemic_guardrail_updated":true,"guardrail_generation":148},
    {"id":"LEARN-PR154-036","pr":154,"source":"external_review","review_comment_id":4019702452,"class_id":"ADV-SEMANTIC-ALLOWLIST-BYPASS","invariant_ids":["INV-BOUNDARY-002","INV-OBS-002"],"root_cause":"Identifier component splitting handled lower-to-upper camel boundaries but not acronym-to-Pascal transitions. Conventional names such as METRICSRepository therefore collapsed into one component and evaded forbidden metric-family matching in code and paths.","horizontal_audit":["acronym-to-word boundaries","all-caps prefixes","Pascal suffixes","code identifiers","path components","plural morphology after splitting"],"guardrails":[{"path":"tools/assurance/test_validate_g1_identity_tenant_shell_authorization.py","probe":"falsify_implementation_scope_gate_execution"}],"systemic_guardrail_updated":true,"guardrail_generation":149},
    {"id":"LEARN-PR154-037","pr":154,"source":"external_review","review_comment_id":4019702458,"class_id":"ADV-SEMANTIC-ALLOWLIST-BYPASS","invariant_ids":["INV-BOUNDARY-002","INV-OBS-002"],"root_cause":"The authorized browser-automation exception was exact-identifier-only. Legitimate browser E2E phrases and compound test identifiers still exposed an automation component and were falsely rejected despite being explicitly inside G2 authority.","horizontal_audit":["browser automation phrase","browserAutomationTest identifier","browser_automation identifier","automation marker boundary","unrelated automation remains forbidden","geometric false-positive regression"],"guardrails":[{"path":"tools/assurance/test_validate_g1_identity_tenant_shell_authorization.py","probe":"falsify_implementation_scope_gate_execution"}],"systemic_guardrail_updated":true,"guardrail_generation":150},
    {"id":"LEARN-PR154-038","pr":154,"source":"external_review","review_comment_id":4020319839,"class_id":"ADV-SEMANTIC-ALLOWLIST-BYPASS","invariant_ids":["INV-BOUNDARY-002","INV-OBS-002"],"root_cause":"The browser-E2E exception masked an entire compound identifier instead of only the authorized browser-plus-automation component pair, allowing an explicitly forbidden suffix such as Metric to disappear from semantic inspection.","horizontal_audit":["browserAutomationMetric suffix preservation","browserAutomationTest authorized regression","browser automation phrase masking","generic Automation exclusion","forbidden suffix component scanning"],"guardrails":[{"path":"tools/assurance/test_validate_g1_identity_tenant_shell_authorization.py","probe":"falsify_implementation_scope_gate_execution"}],"systemic_guardrail_updated":true,"guardrail_generation":151},
    {"id":"LEARN-PR154-039","pr":154,"source":"external_review","review_comment_id":4020319850,"class_id":"ADV-SEMANTIC-ALLOWLIST-BYPASS","invariant_ids":["INV-BOUNDARY-002","INV-OBS-002"],"root_cause":"Compound forbidden markers were matched only as whole identifiers or singleton components, so excluded component sequences embedded inside larger conventional identifiers were not recognized.","horizontal_audit":["executeSourceCutover","sendMonitoringToAlerting","InitialResourceIngestionService","runProductionDeployment","bounded marker subsequences","morphology per component"],"guardrails":[{"path":"tools/assurance/test_validate_g1_identity_tenant_shell_authorization.py","probe":"falsify_implementation_scope_gate_execution"}],"systemic_guardrail_updated":true,"guardrail_generation":152},
    {"id":"LEARN-PR154-040","pr":154,"source":"external_review","review_comment_id":4020319859,"class_id":"ADV-SEMANTIC-ALLOWLIST-BYPASS","invariant_ids":["INV-BOUNDARY-002","INV-OBS-002"],"root_cause":"Persistence-write detection covered simple dot and quoted bracket calls but not semantically equivalent optional chaining, parenthesized receivers, call/apply invocation, static computed member concatenation, or extracted write methods.","horizontal_audit":["database optional chaining","parenthesized persistence receiver","method call and apply","static computed member concatenation","method extraction and later invocation","receiver alias propagation"],"guardrails":[{"path":"tools/assurance/test_validate_g1_identity_tenant_shell_authorization.py","probe":"falsify_implementation_scope_gate_execution"}],"systemic_guardrail_updated":true,"guardrail_generation":153},
    {"id":"LEARN-PR154-041","pr":154,"source":"external_review","review_comment_id":4020319864,"class_id":"ADV-SEMANTIC-ALLOWLIST-BYPASS","invariant_ids":["INV-BOUNDARY-002","INV-OBS-002"],"root_cause":"Raw-secret protection required the secret spelling to remain directly inside a sink expression and did not propagate taint through local aliases or simple helper wrappers, allowing credentials to be exfiltrated after trivial renaming.","horizontal_audit":["secret alias propagation","response helper wrappers","logging and persistence wrappers","direct response sink","opaque credential_binding_ref non-taint regression","transitive local aliases"],"guardrails":[{"path":"tools/assurance/test_validate_g1_identity_tenant_shell_authorization.py","probe":"falsify_implementation_scope_gate_execution"}],"systemic_guardrail_updated":true,"guardrail_generation":154},
